    "nodes": {
      "11": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "EXAMPLE 1: RESOURCE NODES\n\nThere are four nodes that deal with resources.\nEach node accepts their respective resource type from a resource in node.\nMore importantly, you can assign resources through the node panel.\nHere you can also instantiate the node."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 293.8172607421875,
          "width": 655.008056640625,
          "x": 275.48590087890625,
          "y": 96.82210540771484
        },
        "class": {
          "id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
          "version": 1
        },
        "clock": "video",
        "color": "ffff6a00",
        "constants": {},
        "hidden": [
          "text",
          "alignment",
          "font-size",
          "fill"
        ],
        "name": "Group",
        "thumbnail_visible": true
      },
      "12": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": true
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "RESOURCE NODES\n\nThe Resource nodes allow you to assign a resource to them and route it to multiple destinations or instantiate it. \nThese nodes are the \"closed\" brothers of the Resource In nodes.\nAllowing you as a creator to work with resources without exposing them.\n\nThe resource types are paths towards files on your hard drive.\nThis means that they do not take up any memory until used.\nFor example: the LUT node using a LUT 3D resource\nThis means that you can have tons of resources \"ready to go\" only to use them when actually needed."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 229.72769165039062,
          "width": 833.6476440429688,
          "x": 276.40777587890625,
          "y": -157.50588989257812
        },
